; ==============================================================================
; A RUNTIME-WORK BENCHMARK: work whose operands exist only in the process that runs it
; ==============================================================================
; WHY THE CORPUS COULD NOT ANSWER THE QUESTION
; -------------------------------------------
; Almost every suite in `test/` is CLOSED: its operands are literals, so `lin build`
; evaluates the whole numeric cone at build time and the artifact that ships runs in
; ~1 reduce step (the `[aot]` line of `lin build` reports it).  A measurement of what
; a DRIVER spends on RECOGNITION at run time taken over that corpus therefore measures
; almost nothing -- the run-time reduction it would instrument has already happened,
; on the build host, in a different process.  This benchmark is the missing case.
;
; WHAT IT DOES.  `(sumto N)` with N read from the environment: the value of the
; program is decided by the process that RUNS it, so the build cannot bake it.
; Needed order stops at the observation (src/io.c's `lin_build_gate` -- a call no
; provider DECLARED a function of its operands is not performed by a build), the
; residual ships, and the artifact performs the observation AND the whole loop in its
; own process.  Measured at BENCH_N=12: the interpreter runs 19876 reduce steps and
; the artifact 19796 -- the AOT pass moved one step of it.
;
; WHY THIS SHAPE AND NOT SOMETHING FANCIER.  `sumto` is the loop
; test/runtime_ffi.lin and test/build_observe.lin already use, so its values are
; pinned by suites that pass: `(sumto 6)` is 21, `(sumto 30)` is 465.  Every operator
; in it (`add`, `pred`, `is_zero`, `ifl`, the `_cl` operand spine) is one a fold driver
; has to RECOGNIZE on every iteration, which is exactly the cost under measurement --
; a loop built out of pure-Lin dispatch with no `_op` redex in it would run steps
; without ever entering a recogniser, and would measure the wrong thing.
;
; WHAT IT IS NOT.  It is not a `; expect` suite: its answer depends on the environment
; (`BENCH_N`), so a fixed expectation would have to freeze one N.  test/bench_runtime.sh
; is the harness -- it pins the answer against the interpreter at more than one N,
; checks the artifact agrees, and (with the temporary recognition counters compiled in)
; prints the recognition table.  A suite with no `; expect` line is skipped by
; test/run_tests.sh and by test/aot_equiv.py's corpus sweep, which is intended:
; nothing here is asserted about a fixed N.
; ==============================================================================
(load "std/std.lin")

; The loop.  `add` is a saturated `_op` closure (std/num.lin), so each iteration is a
; fold driver's problem: recognize the redex, read the operator index and the operand
; spine, then either compile the cone (native) or resolve the two scalars (arith).
(define! sumto (num -> num) (\n (ifl (is_zero n) (\_ 0) (\_ (add n (sumto (pred n)))))))

; N EXISTS ONLY AT RUN TIME.  ffl(parse_float(getenv "BENCH_N")) is the 3-deep nest
; test/runtime_ffi.lin pins for exactly this reason, and it is what makes the build
; decline: the artifact has to ask its OWN environment.
(sumto (ccall "lin_ffloor" (cons (float.float (ffi.getenv "BENCH_N")) nil)))
